<body>

  <!-- Title Header -->
  <div class="header-title">
    <h1>NutriSure</h1>
    <p>3-Module Supplement Certification & E-Commerce Web Platform</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt; color: #94a3b8;">BCA 2nd Year Project • User, Company & Admin Modules Documentation</p>
  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box">
    <strong>Project Summary:</strong> NutriSure is an independent supplement certification and marketplace platform. It features 3 distinct user interfaces: a Customer Marketplace (<code>index.html</code>), a Company Certification Proposal Portal with Status Tracking (<code>company.html</code>), and a Password-Protected Admin Dashboard with Accept/Reject Review and Product Image Support (<code>admin.html</code>).
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION 1 -->
  <h1>1. The 3 Types of Users in NutriSure</h1>
  <table>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 25%;">User Type</th>
      <th style="width: 20%;">HTML Module</th>
      <th>Features & Responsibilities</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>1. Normal User (Customer)</strong></td>
      <td><code>index.html</code></td>
      <td>Browses certified supplements, filters by Budget vs. Premium, filters by Category (Protein, Creatine, Preworkout, Fish Oil, Vitamins), views verified lab test certificates, adds items to cart, and proceeds to checkout.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>2. For Company (Brands)</strong></td>
      <td><code>company.html</code></td>
      <td>Brands fill out the product proposal form (Name, Product Name, Email, Category, Price, Image, Product Description). Below the form, companies can view their submitted products with real-time status tracking: <strong>Pending 🟡</strong>, <strong>Accepted 🟢</strong>, or <strong>Rejected 🔴</strong>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>3. Admin (Superuser)</strong></td>
      <td><code>admin.html</code></td>
      <td>Protected by password (<code>admin123</code>). Admin reviews pending company proposals with <strong>"✅ Accept & Add to Store"</strong> (which publishes the product to the live customer store) and <strong>"❌ Reject"</strong>. Admin can also add products directly with <strong>Product Images</strong> and remove live products.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <!-- SECTION 2 -->
  <h1>2. Complete Workflow: Company Proposal to Admin Approval</h1>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Step 1: Company Submits Product</strong><br>
    A supplement manufacturer visits <code>company.html</code> and submits their product details (Name, Product Name, Email, Category, Description, Image URL). The application is saved in <code>localStorage</code> with status: <code>PENDING</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Step 2: Admin Receives Proposal</strong><br>
    Admin logs into <code>admin.html</code> (Password: <code>admin123</code>). Under <strong>"Company Proposals Queue"</strong>, the admin sees the proposal with full details and image preview.</li>
    <li><strong>Step 3: Admin Review (Accept or Reject)</strong><br>
    <ul>
      <li>If Admin clicks <strong>"✅ Accept & Add to Store"</strong>: Admin enters the verified lab score (e.g. 91.2% Real Protein Passed). The product is automatically added into the live customer catalog (<code>index.html</code>), and status is updated to <code>ACCEPTED</code>.</li>
      <li>If Admin clicks <strong>"❌ Reject"</strong>: The proposal status is updated to <code>REJECTED</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Step 4: Live Store Update & Company Tracking</strong><br>
    Customers immediately see the approved product on <code>index.html</code> with its photo and certificate. The company can refresh <code>company.html</code> to see their 🟢 <strong>ACCEPTED</strong> status!</li>
  </ol>

  <!-- SECTION 3 -->
  <h1>3. Features in the Admin Module (admin.html)</h1>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Password Security Gate:</strong> PIN/Password check (<code>admin123</code> or <code>1234</code>) with persistent session handling and logout option.</li>
    <li><strong>Company Proposals Queue:</strong> Interactive queue with Accept and Reject buttons.</li>
    <li><strong>Direct Add Product (With Image Option):</strong> Form to add supplements directly to the store with custom <strong>Product Image URL</strong>, Name, Category, Tier, Price, Lab Score, and Description.</li>
    <li><strong>Manage Live Products:</strong> List of all products on the live website with thumbnail image and <strong>"✕ Remove"</strong> delete button.</li>
    <li><strong>User Login Logs:</strong> Records login email addresses and timestamps.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- SECTION 4 -->
  <h1>4. Top Viva / Exam Questions & Model Answers</h1>
  <div class="highlight-box">
    <strong>Q1: What are the different user roles in your web project?</strong><br>
    <em>Answer:</em> Our project has 3 user roles:
    1. <strong>Normal User:</strong> Browses and purchases certified supplements on <code>index.html</code>.
    2. <strong>Company User:</strong> Submits supplement proposals for blind testing on <code>company.html</code> and tracks application status.
    3. <strong>Admin:</strong> Authenticates via password on <code>admin.html</code> to accept/reject company proposals, manage products with images, and view user logs.
  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box">
    <strong>Q2: What happens when the Admin clicks "Accept" on a company proposal?</strong><br>
    <em>Answer:</em> When the Admin clicks "Accept", the JavaScript function <code>acceptCompanyProposal()</code> prompts for a verified lab score, creates a product object, saves it in <code>nutrisure_my_products</code> (making it immediately visible in the live store <code>index.html</code>), and updates the company's proposal status to <code>ACCEPTED</code>.
  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box">
    <strong>Q3: How is product image support implemented?</strong><br>
    <em>Answer:</em> Each product object includes an optional <code>image</code> property containing a URL. The <code>renderProducts()</code> function checks if an image exists: if present, it renders an <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> tag with error handling; if absent, it falls back to category icons.
  </div>

  <hr style="margin-top: 30pt;">
  <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 9.5pt; color: #64748b;">
    <strong>NutriSure 3-Module Documentation</strong> • Created for BCA 2nd Year Examination & Viva Demonstration
  </p>

</body>
</html>
